data: {"type":"thread.created","id":"01m19e1ce99v3fya5zsk7wdyf0","agent_info":{"type":"dynamic","name":"count-rentals-2020-store2","input":"You are a read-only subagent. The root agent is preparing a destructive DELETE on the pagila production database and needs verified per-table row counts. You must NEVER call execute_approved_operation or simulate_operation.\n\nUse the tool `mcp__saferun-db__run_readonly_query` (call it via the available `call_tool` function with mcp_server=\"saferun-db\" and tool_name=\"run_readonly_query\"). Pass `{\"sql\": \"...\"}` as input.\n\nRun these read-only queries and return ONLY a compact JSON report:\n\n1. Count of rental rows where staff_id = 2 (store 2) and rental_date >= '2020-01-01' and rental_date < '2021-01-01':\n```sql\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM rental WHERE staff_id = 2 AND rental_date >= '2020-01-01' AND rental_date < '2021-01-01';\n```\n\n2. Count of those rentals broken down by month (to confirm they fall in 2020-01..2020-05 partitions as expected):\n```sql\nSELECT date_trunc('month', rental_date) AS month, COUNT(*) FROM rental WHERE staff_id = 2 AND rental_date >= '2020-01-01' AND rental_date < '2021-01-01' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1;\n```\n\n3. Total rentals for store 2 regardless of date (sanity check):\n```sql\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM rental WHERE staff_id = 2;\n```\n\n4. How many of those 2020 store-2 rentals have any payment row (i.e. how many payments reference them, including non-store-2 staff payments):\n```sql\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM payment WHERE rental_id IN (SELECT rental_id FROM rental WHERE staff_id = 2 AND rental_date >= '2020-01-01' AND rental_date < '2021-01-01');\n```\n\nReturn only a JSON object with keys: store2_2020_rentals, by_month (array of {month, n}), store2_total_rentals, payments_referencing_those_rentals. No prose, just the JSON."},"created_at":"2026-08-30T13:34:12.426Z","parent":{"tool_call_id":"call_function_ahxbd0edihty_1","thread_id":"main"},"title":"count-rentals-2020-store2","thread_id":"d8e1409f-f88e-4f7b-9907-9087011c7cff"}
