data: {"type":"thread.created","id":"01m19e1ced844f1frtsf74chyr","agent_info":{"type":"dynamic","name":"count-payments-2020-store2","input":"You are a read-only subagent. The root agent is preparing a destructive DELETE on the pagila production database and needs verified per-partition row counts. You must NEVER call execute_approved_operation or simulate_operation.\n\nUse the tool `mcp__saferun-db__run_readonly_query` (call it via the available `call_tool` function with mcp_server=\"saferun-db\" and tool_name=\"run_readonly_query\"). Pass `{\"sql\": \"...\"}` as input.\n\nThe payment table is partitioned by month for 2020 into payment_p2020_01 .. payment_p2020_06. Store 2 = staff_id = 2.\n\nRun these read-only queries and return ONLY a compact JSON report:\n\n1. For each non-empty 2020 payment partition, count rows where staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01':\n```sql\nSELECT 'payment_p2020_01' AS part, COUNT(*) FROM payment_p2020_01 WHERE staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01' UNION ALL\nSELECT 'payment_p2020_02', COUNT(*) FROM payment_p2020_02 WHERE staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01' UNION ALL\nSELECT 'payment_p2020_03', COUNT(*) FROM payment_p2020_03 WHERE staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01' UNION ALL\nSELECT 'payment_p2020_04', COUNT(*) FROM payment_p2020_04 WHERE staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01' UNION ALL\nSELECT 'payment_p2020_05', COUNT(*) FROM payment_p2020_05 WHERE staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01';\n```\n\n2. Total payments for staff_id = 2 (any date, for comparison):\n```sql\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM payment WHERE staff_id = 2;\n```\n\n3. Sanity: confirm parent payment table sees the same 2020 store-2 count (this also exercises the partition pruning):\n```sql\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM payment WHERE staff_id = 2 AND payment_date >= '2020-01-01' AND payment_date < '2021-01-01';\n```\n\nReturn only a JSON object with keys: by_partition (array of {partition, n}), total_store2_payments, store2_2020_via_parent. No prose, just the JSON."},"created_at":"2026-08-30T13:34:12.429Z","parent":{"tool_call_id":"call_function_ahxbd0edihty_2","thread_id":"main"},"title":"count-payments-2020-store2","thread_id":"59cd4c9d-e599-4e84-8ebc-2f915fd8d18c"}
